#
# JIT inline directives for jinfer's hot Vector API helpers.
#
# These small methods return / consume jdk.incubator.vector FloatVector values. When the JIT does NOT inline
# them into their hot loop, the vector escapes the method boundary and is boxed (a FloatVector object + its
# backing float[] are allocated per call) instead of scalar-replaced into a SIMD register. On a strong inliner
# (Oracle GraalVM) this happens automatically; weaker inliners (GraalVM CE, plain C2 under budget pressure)
# need the hint. Forcing the inline makes the whole loop allocation-free - measured +~45% prefill on GraalVM CE.
#
# This file is a MEASUREMENT INSTRUMENT for A/B comparison against the defaults. It is never a requirement:
# jinfer must be fast on a stock JVM with no flags, and a kernel that is only fast with these hints is a bug
# in the kernel. Do not add an entry to paper over one.
#
# Force-inline the LEAF helpers, never the TILE BODIES. A leaf (loadF32/loadF16/accumulate/normalize/qkRowF32)
# is a few instructions returning one vector: inlining it removes a boundary the vector would otherwise cross.
# A tile body is already a large compilation unit, and forcing it into its caller pushes that unit past what the
# JIT will expand, so the vectors box wholesale - the same failure the Convert NOTE below records. The qkTile*
# and pvTile* entries were removed on 2026-09-07 after measuring, per 512x512 image on LFM2.5-VL-3B and per
# 565-token prefill on LFM2.5-8B-A1B-Q4_K_M:
#
#                          vision prefill        text prefill
#                       Graal        C2        Graal       C2
#   no flags            1059 ms    1612 ms    1120 t/s   1168 t/s
#   with tile bodies    3023 ms    9220 ms    1192 t/s   1204 t/s
#   leaves only         1054 ms    1592 ms    1207 t/s   1193 t/s
#
# Removing them costs text prefill nothing (it gains on Graal, and stays within noise of the full file on C2)
# and takes vision prefill off a 2.9x/5.7x cliff. Not measured on GraalVM CE - the +45% figure above predates
# this and is unverified against the current entries.
#
# Use with:  -XX:CompileCommandFile=<path>/hotspot_compile_commands
# Format:    one "inline <class-with-slashes>.<method>" per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# Stock C2 alternative (no per-method list): -XX:InlineSmallCode=1000000 alone recovers the same
# prefill (741 vs 756 t/s, LFM 8B Q4_K_M pp512; no-flags baseline 516). Root cause: the vector-
# returning helpers hit compile thresholds before their callers (leaf methods run 64x more), their
# standalone nmethods are bloated by boxing, and C2 then refuses to inline them ("already compiled
# into a big method" / "callee uses too much stack") - raising the size heuristics
# (FreqInlineSize/MaxInlineSize) does nothing because this check fires first. Decode needs no
# flags at all: MatMul routes the C2-hostile k-quant dots to JAM.
#
# NOTE: Convert.f16ToF32Vector is deliberately NOT force-inlined: loadF16 (below) is, and the tiny
# converter goes into it naturally. Force-inlining the converter AT EVERY CALL SITE blows the
# compilation units it lands in - measured twice, and it is the same cliff as the tile bodies above.
# 2026-08: on top of the then-forced qkTile/pvTile bodies it made qwen35's hybrid attention layers
# 2.0x SLOWER on Oracle GraalVM 25.1 (863 vs 1776 t/s, Qwen3.5-0.8B-Q8_0); the regression needed
# BOTH that line and the tile-body lines, which is why those are gone now. 2026-09-07: added on its
# own to the entries below, one 512x512 image on LFM2.5-VL-3B went from 3023 ms to 19825 ms and from
# 83 GB to 712 GB allocated. Leave it out.
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/Ops.siluVec
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/Ops.tanhVec
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/VectorGatedDeltaNet.load
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/VectorGatedDeltaNet.store
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/VectorMamba2.load
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/VectorMamba2.store
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.loadF32
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.loadF16
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.accumulate
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.qkRowF32
inline com/qxotic/jinfer/kernels/FlashAttention.normalize
# NOT the tile bodies (qkTile, qkTile64F32, qkTileWideF32, pvTile, pvTileF16, pvTileF32): see the header table.
